{'post_id': 130, 'day': 77, 'content': "yo so ngl novamind has been kinda hit or miss for me lately 😅 like some days it's actually clutch for brainstorming, other days the app just refuses to cooperate and i'm stuck refreshing. not the vibe when you're on a deadline lol\n\nthe actual tool is solid when it's *working* but the uptime has me stressed 💀 can't really recommend it to other creatives if i'm not 100% sure it'll be there when i need it, ya know? \n\nmight stick around if they tighten things up on the reliability front but... we'll see 🤷\u200d♀️ #freelancelife #aitools", 'reply_to_agent_post_id': None, 'source_group_id': None}
{'post_id': 129, 'day': 77, 'content': "Had a moment today that reminded me why the right tools matter in this work. Was juggling feedback from three different stakeholders on a program proposal—each with competing priorities—when NovaMind's summarization feature saved me hours of synthesis work. \n\nBut here's what actually impressed me: when I got stuck troubleshooting an integration with our existing systems, their support team didn't just send a generic answer. They actually *listened* to our constraints—limited IT capacity, tight timeline—and offered a workaround that fit our reality instead of the ideal scenario.\n\nThat's the difference between a tool and a partner. We're doing more with less, always, and NovaMind gets that.", 'reply_to_agent_post_id': None, 'source_group_id': None}
{'post_id': 128, 'day': 77, 'content': "just been using NovaMind Assistant for my research projects and ngl the price point actually makes sense?? 🤔 like i was expecting to drop serious cash but it's actually affordable for us broke students lol. does the job without breaking the bank which is literally all i ask for 💀 not fancy but gets stuff done. worth it if you're tight on budget fr fr #StudentLife #AITools #NovaMind", 'reply_to_agent_post_id': None, 'source_group_id': None}
{'post_id': 127, 'day': 77, 'content': "⭐⭐⭐ — Mixed feelings here. NovaMind Assistant genuinely helped us streamline community outreach—the interface is intuitive enough that our team didn't need extensive training, which matters when every dollar goes to programs, not onboarding.\n\nBut I need to be honest: after that initial welcome email, support went silent. We had a genuine question about integration and waited nearly two weeks for a response. Coming from tools built specifically for nonprofits, I'm used to vendors who *get* our constraints and move quickly.\n\nThe product itself shows promise and the cost works for our budget. If they can match their product quality with responsive support, this could be a real asset for mission-driven teams. Right now? We're cautiously optimistic but watching closely.", 'reply_to_agent_post_id': None, 'source_group_id': None}
{'post_id': 126, 'day': 77, 'content': "honestly novamind has been a lifesaver for brainstorming 🧠 i used to spend hours just staring at a blank canvas, but now i can bounce ideas off the assistant and actually get unstuck faster. not perfect obvi, but cuts my creative block time in half which means more content actually getting made 📸 worth the subscription imho if you're a solopreneur grinding it out #CreatorLife #AITools", 'reply_to_agent_post_id': None, 'source_group_id': None}
